1
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:07,691
Open a gold chart on MT5.

2
00:00:08,141 --> 00:00:10,413
At the bottom you see volume bars.

3
00:00:10,863 --> 00:00:12,901
One bar is very big.

4
00:00:13,351 --> 00:00:17,060
You think: a lot of gold was traded here.

5
00:00:17,509 --> 00:00:21,298
But this bar does not tell you how much gold was traded.

6
00:00:21,747 --> 00:00:25,301
It only tells you how many times price changed.

7
00:00:25,750 --> 00:00:29,381
And that difference changes everything in order flow.

8
00:00:30,381 --> 00:00:38,506
Hello, this is episode six of the SPIDER Order Flow series. Module 2 starts today: the volume tools.

9
00:00:38,956 --> 00:00:46,113
Last time we looked at effort and result. Effort means volume. But where does that volume come from?

10
00:00:46,563 --> 00:00:57,169
Three questions today. What is the difference between real volume and tick volume? How far can you trust tick volume? And where do you find real volume for forex and gold?

11
00:00:58,169 --> 00:01:01,878
Real volume means: how much was traded.

12
00:01:02,328 --> 00:01:07,083
500 kilos of tomatoes were sold in the market today. That is today's volume.

13
00:01:07,533 --> 00:01:11,399
In markets it is counted in lots or contracts.

14
00:01:11,848 --> 00:01:16,681
But to count it you need one place where every trade is recorded.

15
00:01:17,131 --> 00:01:19,639
That place is called an exchange.

16
00:01:20,639 --> 00:01:26,908
Shares and futures trade on an exchange. Every trade goes into one register.

17
00:01:27,359 --> 00:01:31,485
But spot forex and gold have no single exchange.

18
00:01:31,936 --> 00:01:36,377
They trade between thousands of banks and brokers, in many different places.

19
00:01:36,827 --> 00:01:38,863
There is no single register.

20
00:01:39,314 --> 00:01:43,101
So nobody knows the real volume of the whole market.

21
00:01:44,101 --> 00:01:47,811
So what is the volume you see on your chart?

22
00:01:48,261 --> 00:01:49,907
It is tick volume.

23
00:01:50,357 --> 00:01:53,988
A tick means: price changing once.

24
00:01:54,437 --> 00:01:59,923
If price changed 200 times in a candle, that candle's tick volume is 200.

25
00:02:00,374 --> 00:02:04,422
Nowhere does it say how much was traded each time.

26
00:02:05,422 --> 00:02:10,830
Behind one tick there could be 0.01 lots, or 100 lots.

27
00:02:11,280 --> 00:02:15,067
Tick volume counts both the same: one.

28
00:02:15,518 --> 00:02:18,679
And this count comes only from your broker's feed.

29
00:02:19,129 --> 00:02:23,178
On another broker, the same candle can show a different tick volume.

30
00:02:24,178 --> 00:02:27,417
So is tick volume useless? No.

31
00:02:27,867 --> 00:02:32,700
When more trades happen in the market, price also changes more often.

32
00:02:33,150 --> 00:02:38,296
So tick volume often rises and falls together with real volume.

33
00:02:38,745 --> 00:02:44,623
So tick volume tells you fairly well when the market is hot and when it is quiet.

34
00:02:45,623 --> 00:02:48,392
But it misleads you in three places.

35
00:02:48,841 --> 00:02:55,033
One: you cannot see size. A big player or many small ones, you cannot tell.

36
00:02:55,483 --> 00:03:03,293
Two: buys and sells are not shown separately. So delta built from tick data is only an estimate.

37
00:03:03,744 --> 00:03:08,577
Three: it is a picture of one broker only, not the whole market.

38
00:03:09,027 --> 00:03:16,027
Order flow tools need real size and real buy-sell data. Tick volume gives neither.

39
00:03:17,027 --> 00:03:20,737
So where do you find real volume? In the futures market.

40
00:03:21,186 --> 00:03:26,516
Gold and currency futures trade on an exchange called the CME.

41
00:03:26,966 --> 00:03:31,876
Every trade is recorded there: how many contracts, and at what price.

42
00:03:32,327 --> 00:03:38,126
And also whether the trade happened at the Bid or the Ask. That is, who was aggressive.

43
00:03:38,576 --> 00:03:42,049
Real order flow tools run on this data.

44
00:03:43,049 --> 00:03:46,132
Every spot chart has a futures sibling.

45
00:03:46,583 --> 00:03:53,113
Gold's future is GC. The Euro's is 6E. The Pound's is 6B.

46
00:03:53,563 --> 00:03:59,126
The Yen's is 6J. But note: it moves opposite to USDJPY.

47
00:03:59,577 --> 00:04:03,548
Because 6J quotes the yen's price in dollars.

48
00:04:03,998 --> 00:04:08,204
The same applies to the futures for USDCAD and USDCHF.

49
00:04:09,204 --> 00:04:15,316
Indices have futures too, like ES for the S&P and NQ for the Nasdaq.

50
00:04:15,766 --> 00:04:20,912
Crypto is different: each exchange there reports its own real volume.

51
00:04:21,912 --> 00:04:28,521
The futures price is slightly different from spot. In gold the gap can be a few dollars.

52
00:04:28,971 --> 00:04:34,692
But both move together. Up together, down together.

53
00:04:35,142 --> 00:04:39,583
So the method is: read order flow on the futures chart.

54
00:04:40,033 --> 00:04:42,541
Take the trade on your spot chart.

55
00:04:42,991 --> 00:04:45,917
Just adjust the level by that gap.

56
00:04:46,917 --> 00:04:51,749
Where can you see this data? Here are some names. This is not a promotion.

57
00:04:52,199 --> 00:04:58,312
TradingView has CME futures charts. On the free plan the data is delayed.

58
00:04:58,762 --> 00:05:08,088
For footprint and order flow, people use platforms like ATAS, Sierra Chart, NinjaTrader, Quantower and Bookmap.

59
00:05:08,538 --> 00:05:12,404
Real-time CME data is usually paid.

60
00:05:12,854 --> 00:05:16,093
But for learning, delayed data is enough.

61
00:05:17,093 --> 00:05:25,687
The tools coming up in this series, volume profile, footprint and delta, work best on real volume.

62
00:05:26,137 --> 00:05:29,611
An estimate of them can be built on tick volume too.

63
00:05:30,061 --> 00:05:34,189
But remember: an estimate is still only an estimate.

64
00:05:35,189 --> 00:05:36,756
So, today's summary.

65
00:05:37,206 --> 00:05:44,050
Real volume means how much was traded. Tick volume means how many times price changed.

66
00:05:44,500 --> 00:05:52,050
Spot forex and gold give you only tick volume. It shows activity, but not size or buy-sell.

67
00:05:52,500 --> 00:05:57,907
Real volume is in futures. Read order flow there, trade on spot.

68
00:05:58,907 --> 00:06:06,378
